<footer class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep text-navy-on">
  {# Global-landmarks skyline (Eiffel Tower, Big Ben, Colosseum, Statue of
     Liberty, etc.) — the real asset admizzeducation.com's own footer
     already ships (public/images/footer-skyline.webp in that repo, both
     sites under the same Admizz Group), pulled in on explicit instruction
     rather than the earlier world-map-dots placeholder. Purely decorative
     ("global reach"), not a business claim, so this is a styling asset,
     not content subject to the never-invent-facts rule. Bottom-anchored,
     full-bleed, low opacity, matching the source site's own treatment. #}
  <img src="/assets/images/brand/footer-skyline.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="2880" height="500" loading="lazy" class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-full h-auto opacity-[0.35] pointer-events-none select-none">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="shell relative py-12 md:py-14">
    {# Badge sits beside the grid (flex), not inside it as a 5th track --
       an earlier version made it a grid column, which squeezed the 4 real
       link columns narrow enough that "Admizz Workforce Solutions"
       wrapped mid-word. Keeping the grid's own 1.3fr/1fr/1fr/1fr
       proportions untouched and letting the badge take its natural width
       alongside fixes that without shrinking real content to make room
       for a decoration. #}
    <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:justify-between gap-10">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr_1fr_1fr] gap-10 md:gap-8 flex-1">

      <div>
        <img src="/assets/images/brand/mark-white.png" alt="{{ site.name }}" width="150" height="45" class="h-10 w-auto mb-5">
        <p class="text-small text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed">{{ site.description }}</p>
        {# Address dropped from this line -- it's the first item in "Get in
           Touch" now, so stating it here too was the same fact twice in
           one footer. "Est." alone still gives the brand block its own
           bit of real, sourced substance (site.json). #}
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted/70">Est. {{ site.founded }}</p>
      </div>

      {# Column headers upgraded from the small-caps mono eyebrow to a
         heavier, larger display weight (reference: admizzeducation.com's
         footer) -- kept as a one-off treatment scoped to this partial
         rather than changing the shared .eyebrow-on-navy class used
         elsewhere sitewide. A size/weight bump alone read too close to
         the links below it (same serif family, small gap) -- added a
         short gold rule under each header, the same "gold as a divider
         mark" device already used sitewide (e.g. The Shift section's
         w-10 h-px bg-gold), so the title is anchored by a marker instead
         of relying on font contrast alone. #}
      <div>
        <span class="block font-display font-bold text-h4 text-navy-on">Our Ventures</span>
        <span class="block mt-2 mb-4 w-8 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          {% for v in ventures %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ v.href }}" class="text-small text-navy-on-muted hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ v.name }}</a>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>

      {# Same 3 destinations navigation.json feeds the header with, minus
         Our Ventures (its own column already, immediately to the left). #}
      <div>
        <span class="block font-display font-bold text-h4 text-navy-on">Company</span>
        <span class="block mt-2 mb-4 w-8 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          {% for item in navigation.main %}
          {% if item.label != "Our Ventures" %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ item.href }}" class="text-small text-navy-on-muted hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ item.label }}</a>
          </li>
          {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
          {# Press isn't in navigation.main -- that array also drives the
             header's primary nav, and a press/media-kit page doesn't
             belong at that level of prominence. Footer-only link, same
             treatment as the other Company items. #}
          <li>
            <a href="/press/" class="text-small text-navy-on-muted hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">Press</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span class="block font-display font-bold text-h4 text-navy-on">Get in Touch</span>
        <span class="block mt-2 mb-4 w-8 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-small text-navy-on-muted">
          <li>{{ site.address }}</li>
          <li><a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}" class="hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ site.phone }}</a></li>
          <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ site.email }}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

      {# ICEF's own official live badge widget, not a hand-built replica.
         Account #6499 is the exact same accreditation already verified
         against ICEF's public API (docs/01-AUDIT.md §2) and linked from
         the hero — this renders ICEF's real, self-updating seal instead
         of us reproducing their mark by hand. The loader script lives
         once in base.njk (site-wide, lazyOnload-equivalent), matching
         admizzeducation.com's own integration exactly. Falls back to
         nothing (no layout shift) if the 3rd-party script fails to load —
         it renders into this span itself, no placeholder needed. #}
      <div class="shrink-0 lg:self-start" data-icef-badge>
        <span id="iasBadge" data-account-id="6499"></span>
      </div>

    </div>

    {# Bottom bar no longer restates the columns above (it used to repeat
       "Our Ventures" as a link right below its own full column). Legal
       links (2026-09-08: privacy/terms/cookies/sources are now real pages
       -- this comment used to say they weren't and to not invent
       placeholders for them; that's why they land here and not earlier).
       "Back to top" is a genuine, working utility: a plain hash link to
       <main id="main-content"> (base.njk), so it works identically whether
       Lenis is driving smooth scroll or a reduced-motion visitor gets a
       native jump. #}
    <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-white/10 flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-start lg:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <p class="text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide">&copy; {% year %} {{ site.legalName }}. All rights reserved.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <a href="/privacy/" class="text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms/" class="text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">Terms</a>
        <a href="/cookies/" class="text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">Cookies</a>
        <a href="/sources/" class="text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">Sources</a>
        <a href="#main-content" class="group flex items-center gap-2 text-label text-navy-on-muted/80 uppercase tracking-wide hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">
          Back to top
          <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="-rotate-90 transition-transform duration-press ease-signature group-hover:-translate-y-0.5"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
